  "id": "6e728dac-000f-5cc8-9479-93aed9e522a0",
  "slug": "shredded-beef-sliders-recipe-12014089",
  "name": "Shredded Beef Sliders",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "These shredded beef sliders are cheesy, pull-apart sliders with super-tender, slow-braised beef chuck. Red wine, tomato paste, carrot, celery, onion, and garlic create the beautifully flavored sauce.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 275 degrees F (135 degrees C) with rack in the middle position. Heat oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add beef and cook, turning occasionally, until beef is well browned on 2 sides, 16 to 20 minutes. Transfer to a bowl, leaving drippings in the Dutch oven."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add onion, carrots, and celery, and cook over medium-high, stirring occasionally, until slightly softened, about 8 minutes. Add tomato paste and garlic; cook, stirring constantly, until tomato paste turns a shade darker, about 1 minute. Add wine, scraping up any browned bits stuck to bottom of Dutch oven with a wooden spoon. Bring to a simmer over medium-high. Simmer, stirring often, until reduced by half and mixture thickens, about 3 minutes. Return beef, along with any accumulated juices, to Dutch oven and add stock and bay leaf. Bring to a simmer over medium-high. Cover and braise in preheated oven until beef is pull-apart tender, 2 hours 30 minutes to 2 hours 45 minutes. Stir in salt."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Using a slotted spoon, transfer beef mixture to a large bowl. Using 2 forks, pull roast into shreds and lightly moisten with some of the cooking liquid."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Increase oven temperature to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Arrange bottom halves of rolls in a 9x13-inch baking dish. Top evenly with shredded beef, then Cheddar slices. Place top halves of rolls on top. Stir together butter and parsley in a small bowl until combined. Brush butter mixture evenly over tops of rolls."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until rolls are toasted on top and cheese is melted, about 12 minutes."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 165,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 50,
